It is indeed cost-efficient to use AWS Spot instances to save on cost and take advantage of unused EC2 capacity. If you want to use it for ROSA then you need to create a machinepool with the following configuration:

```json
{
  "id": "spottest",
  "instance_type": "m5.xlarge",
  "replicas": 3,
  "aws": {
    "use_spot_instances": true,
    "spot_market_options": {
      "max_price": 0.0646
    }
  }
}
```

Save this configuration to a file (e.g., `spot.json`) and invoke the API by running:
`ocm post /api/clusters_mgmt/v1/clusters/<cluster_id>/machine_pools <<< $(cat spot.json)`
